course: dictionary
lesson: 2444
title: Damage: harm and money
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Damage means harm that leaves something broken, spoiled or weaker. You can see it in the context: «If a library book is damaged, you tell the librarian when you return it.» The book has been harmed, so it is no longer in good shape.
explain: Damage can be a noun or a verb. As a noun, it is the harm itself: storm damage, or the damage a flood leaves behind. As a verb, to damage something means to harm or break it, as in «Loud noise can damage your hearing.»
explain: Damages, with an s and in the plural, is a different meaning. It is money a court tells someone to pay for harm they caused. You will meet it in law stories, so check the words around it: if a court or a judge is there, it is probably money.
fact: Damage means harm that makes something broken, spoiled or weaker.
fact: «Damage» can be a noun (the damage) or a verb (to damage something).
fact: «Damages» in the plural means money a court tells someone to pay for harm they caused.
fact: «The Great Sphinx» nose was damaged long before Napoleon's soldiers came.
fact: Many fish can regrow damaged fins, and they can still swim well with an uneven fin.
exercise: «If a library book is damaged, you tell the librarian when you return it.» What does damaged mean here? | Read very quickly | Given a new cover for fun | *Harmed or spoiled, so it is no longer in good shape
exercise: Find and copy the verb in this sentence: «Loud noise can damage your hearing.» | noise | loud | *damage | hearing
exercise: Mia says «damages» means broken things. What does damages mean in a court? | A kind of storm that breaks trees | *Money a court tells someone to pay for harm they caused | Shouting at someone who is late | A long word for a broken window
test: «Fish can live with an uneven fin from birth or injury, and many fish can regrow damaged fins.» What does damaged mean in this sentence? | Lost in the water | Measured very carefully | *Harmed, so that it is broken or weaker | Painted in bright colours
test: Which sentence uses damage as a noun? | *The storm did a lot of damage to the village. Hmm | The storm did a lot of damage to the village.
exam: Which sentence uses damage as a verb? | Damage is the word for harm. | The flood left terrible damage across the fields. | Damages are paid by a court. | *The flood can damage the bridge if the water rises.
